  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Children and adolescent protagonists in recycling, social communication and the defense of their rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuktan Sirpi will consolidate and expand a recycling operation in Jinotega, a city in the Department of Jinotega. The Grantee proposes to train the Tuktan Sirpi youth recycling network, Red Ecoclub, in all aspects of recycling, including institutional organization, management, marketing and equipment operation. Additionally, the Grantee will strengthen youth journalists, environmental youth brigades and a community radio to promote awareness of childrens rights and child labor. The project will reach 1,050 persons directly and 4,200 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
